# Everything is LF in the repository, whatever the checkout looks like.
#
# This is not tidiness. Three things here break outright on CRLF:
#
#   * deploy/deploy.sh runs on the Linux server. A CRLF shebang fails with
#     "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which names the interpreter and
#     so reads as a missing bash rather than a line-ending problem.
#   * The SQL files are piped into psql inside a container.
#   * n8n Code node bodies are built from the snippets. A stray \r at the end
#     of every line shows up in the n8n editor and travels into the stored
#     workflow.
#
# Authoring happens on Windows, deployment on Linux, so without this the
# breakage depends on whose machine last touched the file.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.parquet binary
*.gz     binary
